{
  "about": "Font, Fill and Borders follow every rule the Number Format and the Alignment follow (ADR-0071, SH-38): insertion and deletion move them, an inserted row or column copies the one before it but for its Borders, an ExSheet-to-ExSheet copy, Ctrl+D, Ctrl+R and the fill handle carry them, Delete keeps them, and each operation is one undo step that puts them back exactly. A copy writes the target's own four sides and a structural edit moves each cell with its own, and the edge two cells share shows the upper or left cell's line where both record one (the twelfth Windows run, cases 12-1 to 12-13). Transcribed from CellFormatCarryTests.cs.",
